---
title: Brown Stew Chicken
servings: 4
course: dinner
cuisine: Jamaican
tags: chicken, simmered, dairy-free
image: https://www.themealdb.com/images/media/meals/sypxpx1515365095.jpg
source: http://www.geniuskitchen.com/recipe/authentic-jamaican-brown-stew-chicken-347996
---

Squeeze @lime{1} over @chicken thigh{6}(whole) and rub well. Drain off excess lime juice.

Combine @tomato{1}(chopped), scallion, @onion{2}(chopped), @garlic clove{2}(chopped), @red pepper{1}(chopped)|pepper, @thyme{2%tsp}, @allspice{1%tsp}|pimento and @soy sauce{2%tbsp} in a large #bowl{} with the @&chicken thigh{} pieces. Cover and marinate at least ~{1%hour}.

Heat @vegetable oil{1%tbsp}|oil in a dutch #pot{} or large #saucepan{}. Shake off the seasonings as you remove each piece of @&chicken thigh{} from the marinade. Reserve the marinade for sauce.

Lightly brown the @&chicken thigh{} a few pieces at a time in very hot oil. Place browned chicken pieces on a #plate{} to rest while you brown the remaining pieces.

Drain off excess oil and return the @&chicken thigh{} to the #saucepan{}. Pour the marinade over the chicken and add the @carrot{1}(chopped)|carrots. Stir and cook over medium heat for ~{10%minutes}.

Mix @cornflour{2%tsp}|flour and @coconut milk{500%ml} and add to stew, stirring constantly. Turn heat down to minimum and cook another ~{20%minutes} or until tender.
